schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: "What Is ReFi?"
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: concept
  summary: >-
    A plain-language introduction to Regenerative Finance for community
    organizers and growers new to crypto: the "money that builds soil
    instead of mining it" framing, three concrete problem/solution pairs
    (Silvi for proving impact, Gitcoin quadratic funding for
    community-driven grants, local tokens for keeping value circulating),
    the carbon-tokenization example with its Verra greenwashing caution, the
    proof-of-stake energy-use correction, and honest limitations.
  audience: "community organisers and growers new to crypto"
  known_tensions:
    - "pricing nature in vs. commodifying/greenwashing risk (the Verra episode)"
    - "crypto energy-use reputation (Bitcoin proof-of-work) vs. actual footprint of the Ethereum/Celo-based tools ReFi mostly uses"
  related_concepts:
    - regenerative-finance-refi
  related_resources:
    - "Toucan Protocol"
    - "Gitcoin (Quadratic Funding)"
    - "Silvi"
    - "Greenpill Network"
  maturity: raw
  public_use: source-linked-unreviewed
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/what-is-refi.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
